# Build-context excludes for the repo-root context (Dockerfile.build, the
# compose `builder` service). That Dockerfile COPYs nothing — the repo is
# volume-mounted at runtime — so the context upload is pure overhead; without
# this file every builder image build ships ~1.6G to the docker daemon.
# The infra/torii-* images use their own directories as context and are
# unaffected by this file.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
target
**/target
frontend/.next
site/.next
bindings
